I don't know why people are suggesting leather gloves and a robe when
you're a samurai.  When you're a samurai, you're not going to be doing
much spellcasting.  If you find a robe, keep it, but don't wear it
unless you're trying to cast a spell.  Out of protection and 
displacement, both are good, I'd consider it kindof a toss up.
And wear those gauntlets of power at least until you get 18/** 
strength.

To repeat something that's already been said, you need magic
resistance as soon as possible.  that's very important.

For weapons I'd use Frost Brand and a silver saber, if you don't have
a silver saber, then go with the +3 katana as your secondary weapon and
find a silver saber.  There aren't all that many things which are cold
resistant until you start seeing the tougher angelic beings.
Fire brand is useless in Ghennom, almost everything there is fire
resistant.  


